Package: libqe
Title: Shared C++ Core for Quantitative Ethnography Packages
Type: Package
Author: Cody L Marquart [aut, cre]
Authors@R: c(person("Cody L", "Marquart", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "cody.marquart@wisc.edu", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3387-6792")))
Maintainer: Cody L Marquart <cody.marquart@wisc.edu>
Version: 0.1.6
Description: Header-only C++ library providing shared computational primitives for
    quantitative ethnography packages (rENA, tma, and others). Canonical headers
    live in include/libqe/ at the repository root; the configure script copies them
    into inst/include/libqe/ at install time so R packages can consume them via
    LinkingTo. Python and Julia bindings point directly at include/libqe/. Exposes
    modules for adjacency vector utilities, normalization, ENA modeling and node
    positioning, stanza/tensor-based accumulation, door temporal pooling,
    trajectory curve analysis, and stability metrics. Also exports Rcpp-wrapped
    versions of every function for direct use and testing in R.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/epistemic-analytics/libqe
BugReports: https://github.com/epistemic-analytics/libqe/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Imports:
    Rcpp
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 2.1.0)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
NeedsCompilation: yes
